 "derivation":"dažaiti is impeccable: Young Avestan dažaiti '(it) burns' (Y.71.8), from *daj-ia-, the ja-present of Proto-Iranian *daj- < PIE *dʰegʷʰ-; Pokorny 240 pairs it with Skt. dáhati and Lith. degù, Cheung 2007 s.v. *daj lists it first, and Klein s.v. 'day' cites 'Avestic dazaiti, “burns”' on the very page (404) Nourai gives. 'vi-dâz “to melt”' is another matter: there is no Avestan vī-daž-. Bartholomae records only apa-daž- and ham-daz- as preverbal compounds of daž- (Cheung s.v. *daj lists the same two and no *ui-), and a grep of the Altīranisches Wörterbuch for vi-daž/vīdāz returns nothing. What exists is Middle Persian widāxtan / widāz- 'to melt', which Nourai has back-projected into Avestan with an Avestan-looking hyphen; and that Middle Persian verb is assigned by Nyberg and Cheung not to daž- 'burn' but to *taH(č) 'to melt' (see node 7). So the node is half confirmed, half a construct, and the half that carries the Persian branch is the constructed half.",
